forti-hole (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Program
    - Rewrite of forti-hole in C++23 on forti-api 1.3 and the forti engine
      (forti-cli 0.6.0, compiled in): /usr/bin/forti-hole with setup, doctor,
      compile, plan, sync, status, pause, resume, attach, detach, remove,
      import pihole and migrate.
    - List pipeline: parallel conditional downloads (https, file), plausibility
      checks (HTML, declared counts, shrink guard) with a last good copy;
      adblock, hosts, domains, wildcard and subtree-domains parsers; canonical
      names with punycode; deduplication across sources and tiers; subtree
      collapse; allow, regex allow and block entries; strict and opt-in compact
      FortiOS encodings; deterministic feeds with SHA-256 and stable hash
      partitions.
    - Budgets: the device-wide domain-entry limit and predicted memory (learned
      bytes per line, red threshold), checked on the compiled set; hagezi TIF
      variant selection (auto: medium, else mini).
    - Sync: push-mode feeds and DNS filter profiles with an ownership marker,
      categories kept per group, deltas in rounds of one request per feed,
      verification by counts and sampled entries, a journal for interrupted
      runs, obsolete feeds removed after their replacements verify.
    - Safety: a two-layer write allowlist (operation check and a guard
      transport under the engine); operator objects are never modified;
      policies change only with attach/detach.
  * Packaging
    - Debian package (amd64) and Homebrew formula; systemd user service and
      timer (installed, never enabled); launchd template; agent skill; example
      configuration.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:19:19 +0000
